 "notes": "Spread pages 116 (left, printed annotations) and 117 (right, ledger grid). Year 1939 throughout (Jan 23 - Mar 7); no mid-chart year change. Group labels U.S. STEEL / BETHLEHEM STEEL / KEY PRICE printed on the DATE line. Column order within each group: SR, NR, UT, DT, NRC, SRC.\n\nCHECKSUM: KP = US + BS holds on every row where all three exist (e.g. Jan 23: 57 7/8 + 63 3/4 = 121 5/8; Jan 31: 59 1/2 + 68 1/2 = 128; Feb 17: 61 1/8 + 71 1/4 = 132 3/8; Feb 25: 63 3/4 + 74 3/4 = 138 1/2). All four carried-forward header groupings also checksum exactly.\n\nHEADER row C is a genuine cross-column (mixed trend-state) situation confirmed by both pixel-color sampling and x-centroid measurement: US 70 is blue pencil in NATURAL RALLY (US had only rallied, not exceeding its prior UT top of 71 1/4), while BS 80 and KP 150 are black ink measured in the UPWARD TREND column (same x as 77 5/8 / 148 7/8). Key-price identity still holds: 70 + 80 = 150. I initially expected all three in NR, but position+color are decisive that BS/KP are UT.\n\nOnly hand-drawn underlines reported: red single underlines under the 9 carried pivotal header figures (rows A/B/C), and a black DOUBLE underline under the Jan 26 downward-trend lows (53 1/4 / 60 1/4 / 113 1/2). The 1939/DATE-line SRC figures (62, 69 1/2, 131 1/2) are not underlined. Printed grid lines (thin blue, periodic red spanning full width) are not treated as underlines.\n\nBlank dated rows with no handwritten entries (27, SAT.28, 30, FEB.1, 3, 7, 8, 9, 10, SAT.11, 14, 15, 20, 21, 23, 27, MAR.1, 2, 6, 7) are omitted per instructions. Note Feb 13 and Feb 22 are absent from the date column (NYSE holidays: Lincoln's and Washington's Birthday), consistent with the Mon-Sat trading calendar.",
